Pasal45

(1) Pelayanan rehabilitasi sosial bagi Perempuan dan Anak korban kekerasan ditujukan untuk memulihkan dan mengembangkan kemampuan korban yang mengalami disfungsi sosial untuk dapat melaksanakan fungsi sosialnya dalam masyarakat secara wajar.

(2) Pelayanan rehabilitasi sosial sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) meliputi: a. pelayanan konseling;

b. penyediaan rumah aman;

c. bimbingan rohani.

(3) Penyelenggaraan pelayanan sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (2) diselenggarakan oleh:

a. Perangkat Daerah yang mempunyai tugas dan berfungsi di bidang sosial; b. DPPPA;
c. P2TP2A;
d. Women Crisis Centre (WeC);
e. organisasi kemasyarakatan bidang sosial; dan/ atau
f. instansi keagamaan.

translated_text:
Article45

(1) Social rehabilitation services for Women and Children victims of violence are aimed at restoring and developing the capacity of victims who experience social dysfunction to be able to carry out their social functions in society properly.

(2) Social rehabilitation services as referred to in paragraph (1) include: a. counseling services;

b. provision of safe houses;

c. spiritual guidance.

(3) The provision of services as referred to in paragraph (2) is organized by:

a. Regional Apparatus having duties and functions in the social field; b. DPPPA;
c. P2TP2A;
d. Women Crisis Centre (WeC);
e. community organizations in the social field; and/or
f. religious institutions.

text:
Pasal46

(1) Pelayanan konseling sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 45 ayat (2) huruf a bertujuan:

a. membantu korban mengenali permasalahannya dan menemukan cara cara yang efektif untuk mengatasinya sendiri;
b. memberdayakan korban untuk menentukan masa depannya;
c. memberikan dukungan moral bagi korban dalam menghadapi proses yang dijalaninya; dan
d. membuat korban merasa diterima di lingkungan masyarakat. 25
(2) Pelayanan konseling dilakukan oleh petugas rehabilitasi sosial yang responsif gender, terdiri atas:
a. konselor;
b. psikolog; dan
c. psikiater.
(3) Pelayanan konseling dilakukan di tempat yang menjamin rasa aman, nyaman dan kerahasiaan informasi dari korban.
(4) Tahapan pelayanan konseling meliputi:
a. konseling awal;
b. konseling lanjutan;
c. pembahasan kasus (Case conference); dan
d. kunjungan ke lokasi (home visit).

translated_text:
Article46

(1) Counseling services as referred to in Article 45 paragraph (2) letter a aim to:

a. help victims identify their problems and find effective ways to overcome them themselves;
b. empower victims to determine their future;
c. provide moral support for victims in facing the process they are undergoing; and
d. make victims feel accepted in the community environment. 25
(2) Counseling services are carried out by social rehabilitation officers who are gender responsive, consisting of:
a. counselors;
b. psychologists; and
c. psychiatrists.
(3) Counseling services are conducted in places that guarantee a sense of security, comfort and confidentiality of information from victims.
(4) The stages of counseling services include:
a. initial counseling;
b. follow-up counseling;
c. case discussion (Case conference); and
d. site visits (home visit).

